      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what checks do we actually want here? Should we be checking texture/renderability here as well? If we do that here, what checks should go into the creation of a GrSurfaceProxy? Do we want to get to a place where a GrColorType is not passed into GrSurfaceProxy factories at all? In that case do we need a way to just generically check if that GrBackendFormat can be a texture or rendered to (in GL\u0027s case the rendered to would just mean FBO attachable). Then when making a surface context we\u0027ll call into caps again but this time with a GrColorType and make sure the combination is texturable and renderable?\n\nOr do we think some of this should have all been checked at a higher level and we should just be making asserts down in here?",
      "range": {
